## 5. Known Windows pitfalls

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Python import of pandas/openalgo hangs forever in background jobs | `platform.machine()` shells out to `cmd /c ver` with no console | launch via `run_server.py` (pre-seeds the probes) |
| Engine discovery hangs | `market/sqlite_downloader.py` had module-level `while True` | fixed 2026-10-07 (guarded behind `__main__`) |
| Dashboard EOFError on boot | `market/ieod.py` ran `input()` at import | fixed 2026-10-07 (guarded behind `__main__`) |
| Duplicate `run_server.py` / `websocket_proxy` processes accumulate | detached `Start-Process` launches without killing the old PID first | kill by command-line match before relaunch (see §6) |

## 6. Full-stack start / restart (verified 2026-10-08)

Run this when the three services are down or duplicated. Order matters:
OpenAlgo first (the engine reads its mode at boot), dashboard last.

```powershell
$R = "C:\Users\Admin\CodeGPT\my-trading-system"
# 1. Stop any stale instances (match the command line, never a blind kill).
Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "Name='python.exe'" |
  Where-Object { $_.CommandLine -like '*run_server.py*' -or
                 $_.CommandLine -like '*start_openalgo*' -or
                 $_.CommandLine -like '*websocket_proxy*' } |
  ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_.ProcessId -Force }
Start-Sleep -Seconds 4
# 2. OpenAlgo (5000 + 8765).
$env:APP_MODE = "standalone"
Start-Process cmd -ArgumentList "/c start /B $R\.venv\Scripts\python.exe $R\scripts\start_openalgo.py --no-scrub-on-exit"
Start-Sleep -Seconds 40
# 3. Dashboard (8050).
Start-Process -FilePath "$R\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" `
  -ArgumentList "$R\Blue_engine\dashboard\run_server.py" -WorkingDirectory $R `
  -RedirectStandardOutput "$R\logs\dash_dmc.log" -RedirectStandardError "$R\logs\dash_dmc_err.log"
```

